{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"28ac49b7bbca3da33c0cf0228504a0447c8e375391f57c6e9b4758c1c0c5f155","packTokens":2393,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":299,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":616,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1372,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build a web app for Hive Works with two screens: a filtered requests list and request detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Store requests with the specified fields and validation, persistence, and exactly 8 seeded requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide exactly four API operations: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Enforce request validation, initial Open status, allowed status transitions, and immutable fields with no deletion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement the list screen, status filters, creation dialog, loading/empty/error states, and responsive request rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement request detail, status actions, update failure behavior, and not-found behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Apply the specified light visual design, accessible controls, badges, and responsive layouts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Add automated business-rule tests and the specified end-to-end workflow test.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should leading/trailing whitespace be handled for title and description validation and storage?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim leading/trailing whitespace before validation and storage; treat a resulting blank title as missing.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No additional browser commitment; target a modern browser.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If multiple requests have the same creation timestamp, how should their relative order be determined in the newest-first list?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Their relative order is unspecified and may vary.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"If creating a request fails for a reason other than field validation (for example, a network or server error), what should the dialog do?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show a generic creation error, keep the dialog open with its values, and allow another submission.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"If loading a detail address fails for a reason other than an unknown ID, what should the detail screen show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show a generic loading error with a Retry action; reserve “Request not found.” for unknown IDs.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"When the app starts with an already-populated database, how should the eight seed requests be handled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Insert the eight seed requests only when initializing an empty database; preserve all requests on restarts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"After successfully creating a request while a status filter other than All is selected, what should happen to the filter and list?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When the user follows the detail screen's Back link, should the list retain the previously selected status filter?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain the filter selected before opening the detail screen.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Hive Works maintenance app with exactly two screens, Requests and Request detail, for demo user Sam Carter (SC), without sign-in or role selection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Define only maintenance request records with a system-generated ID, UTC creation timestamp, required title, area, priority, and status, and optional description; trim title and description before validation and storage, and reject blank titles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Validate titles at 3–80 characters, supported areas (Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, Reception), priorities (Low, Normal, Urgent), and supplied descriptions at no more than 500 characters, returning messages that name invalid fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"On creation, set status to Open and assign the ID and UTC creation timestamp regardless of caller-supplied system-controlled values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"On empty-database initialization, insert exactly eight seed requests: four Open (including one Urgent), two In progress, and two Done, representing every supported area; preserve existing requests and insert no seeds when the database is nonempty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests with an optional single-status filter, create, get by ID, and change status; prevent changes to title, area, priority, and description after creation, and expose no deletion operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Return all requests or only those matching the optional status filter, ordered newest first by creation timestamp without guaranteeing order for equal timestamps; return a matching record by ID or report not found.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status changes, and reject other transitions without changing stored status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"On Requests, show the Hive Works wordmark, SC, mutually exclusive All, Open, In progress, and Done filters with All selected by default, and a New request button.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show each matching request's title, area, priority and status badges, and UTC creation date in date-only form, newest first; open its detail screen when selected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Open a creation dialog from New request with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, supported Area and Priority values, Normal selected by default, and Create and Cancel buttons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When creation validation fails, keep the dialog open and show each field's validation message beneath that field; on successful creation, close the dialog, show the new Open request at the top, and select All if another filter was active.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"While creation is pending, disable Create and prevent duplicate calls; for non-validation failures, show a generic error, retain entered values and the open dialog, and allow another submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Show “Loading requests…” while the list loads, “No requests here.” when empty, or “Could not load requests.” and Retry on failure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"On Request detail, show a Back link, title, area, priority and status badges, UTC creation date in date-only form, and the description or “No description.”; Back returns to Requests with its prior filter retained.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests; update the status badge and next action only after a successful status change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"On status-update failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the previously displayed status and action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown request ID, show “Request not found.” and a link to Requests; for other detail-loading failures, show a generic error with Retry, not “Request not found.”.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Use one light theme with a neutral background, near-black text, one primary-button brand color, one sans-serif font, blue Open badges, amber In progress badges, green Done badges, red Urgent badges, and neutral Low and Normal badges; show text on every badge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Meet WCAG AA contrast thresholds and provide labeled fields and keyboard-reachable controls; show stacked request cards at 375 px and a request table at 1280 px, without horizontal page scrolling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated tests for creation and validation, allowed and disallowed status transitions, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID handling, plus an end-to-end create, detail, status-change, and filter workflow test.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Deploy the app in one cloud region in the client's cloud account.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}